# Project 2: The Server Commander

## DecodeLabs Cloud Computing Internship

### Project Overview

The Server Commander is a cloud infrastructure project completed as part of the DecodeLabs Cloud Computing Internship.

The objective of this project was to launch, secure, and configure a Linux-based virtual server on AWS. The server was accessed securely using SSH, configured with the Nginx web server, and used to host a custom webpage.

---

## Project Objective

The main objective of this project was to gain practical experience with cloud server deployment and administration.

The project involved:

* Launching an Amazon EC2 virtual machine
* Configuring a Security Group for secure network access
* Connecting to the Linux server using SSH
* Installing and configuring the Nginx web server
* Hosting a custom "Welcome to DecodeLabs" webpage
* Accessing the deployed website through the EC2 public IPv4 address

